      "summaries": {
        "en": "Video2x is an open-source framework that enhances video quality through super-resolution and frame interpolation, making old or low-resolution footage look sharper and smoother. It achieves this by leveraging multiple neural network models like Real-ESRGAN and RIFE, allowing users to choose the best approach for their specific content. You can use it via command-line tools to upscale anime, restore archival videos, or create smoother slow-motion effects by processing video files directly on your computer.",
        "zh": "Video2x是一个基于机器学习的开源视频处理框架，专注于通过超分辨率和帧插值技术提升视频质量，让老旧或低清素材变得清晰流畅。它巧妙整合了多种神经网络模型（如Real-ESRGAN、RIFE），用户可根据内容类型选择最适合的算法——例如用Real-CUGAN处理动漫、用RIFE生成平滑慢动作。该工具提供命令行接口，支持本地处理视频文件，适合用于修复历史影像、增强动画细节或制作高质量慢镜头，开发者还可通过其模块化设计集成新模型来扩展功能。",
        "es": "Video2x is an open-source framework that enhances video quality through super-resolution and frame interpolation, making old or low-resolution footage look sharper and smoother. It achieves this by leveraging multiple neural network models like Real-ESRGAN and RIFE, allowing users to choose the best approach for their specific content. You can use it via command-line tools to upscale anime, restore archival videos, or create smoother slow-motion effects by processing video files directly on your computer.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "video2x stands out for anime4k, frame-interpolation, and machine-learning in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Video2x is an open-source framework that enhances video quality through super-resolution and frame interpolation, making old or low-resolution footage look sharper and smoother. It achieves this by leveraging multiple neural network models like Real-ESRGAN and RIFE, allowing users to choose the best approach for their specific content. You can use it via command-line tools to upscale anime, restore archival videos, or create smoother slow-motion effects by processing video files directly on your computer.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/k4yt3x/video2x for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
